 r←IsSafeRelativePath path;segments
⍝ Returns 1 when `path`, a relative path taken from a request, cannot lead outside the folder
⍝ it is appended to, and 0 otherwise.
⍝ Strict on purpose, because whoever sends the request writes the path:
⍝ * Only "/" separates folders. A backslash is refused because Windows takes it for a
⍝   separator as well.
⍝ * No segment may consist of nothing but dots and blanks. That covers "..", and ".. " and
⍝   "..." too: Windows drops trailing dots and blanks from a name.
⍝ * No colon and no control character: on Windows those lead to drives, alternate data
⍝   streams and devices.
 r←0
 :If ~∨/path∊'\:',⎕UCS ¯1+⍳32
     segments←'/'(≠⊆⊢)path
     r←~∨/{∧/⍵∊'. '}¨segments
 :EndIf
